#Lesson focus is on loops - Loops allow you to execute a block of code multiple times, which is useful for tasks that require repetition

#1 First type of loop command is "While"

#The "While" loop continues to execute the block of code as long as the condition is true (again and again) - once the condition is false the loop stops executing
#The "While" loop is used when you do not know how many times you want to execute a block of code
#You are responsible for creating a condition that will eventually become false - otherwise the loop continues to execute forver

#2 Second type of loop command is "For"

#The "For" loop continues to execute the block of code for each item in a sequence (list, string, range, etc.) - once the loop has iterated over all items in the sequence it stops executing 
#The "For" loop is used to execute a block of code a specific number of times - when you know how many times to execute the block of code
#The "For" loop automatically processes the sequence/next items   

#We can use additional commands to control the flow of a loop 
#Break - stops the loop 
#Continue - skips the rest of the code in the loop and goes to the next iteration of the loop
#Return - stops the loop and returns a value to the calling function (if applicable) - this is used in functions to return a value to the main function or calling function

#We can use the while true command to create an infinite loop until a condition is met - we can then use the break command to stop the loop and move onto the next line of code
